nsh2405/bi-gram-word-suggestion","stars":1,"forks":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":2300,"global_rank":107127},{"name":"segerphilip/HackMIT2015","owner":"segerphilip","html_url":"https://github.com/segerphilip/HackMIT2015","stars":1,"forks":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Team: Byron, Keenan, Patrick, and Philip","topics":[],"score":2300,"global_rank":107134},{"name":"0xhmn/daily-trade","owner":"0xhmn","html_url":"https://github.com/0xhmn/daily-trade","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2300,"global_rank":107142},{"name":"bruceoberg/flickr-feedr","owner":"bruceoberg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruceoberg/flickr-feedr","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"feed a flat flickr export directory (from zips) into apple's photo app with exif data. also put images in appropriate folders from flickr.","topics":[],"score":2300,"global_rank":107155},{"name":"truont2/Tsunagu","owner":"truont2","html_url":"https://github.com/truont2/Tsunagu","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Mental Health Appliction","topics":[],"score":2300,"global_rank":107157},{"name":"srzer/cse-507-project","owner":"srzer","html_url":"https://github.com/srzer/cse-507-project","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","descript